Source: zyphoros-base
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Admin <admin@zyphoros.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: zyphoros-base
Architecture: all
# Depends: the system is broken without these. Removing one removes this
# meta-package too, and the desktop meta-packages that depend on it.
Depends: zyphoros-branding,
         linux-image-amd64,
         systemd-sysv,
         libpam-systemd,
         dbus,
         systemd-timesyncd,
         network-manager,
         sudo,
         locales,
         keyboard-configuration,
         console-setup,
         tzdata,
         iproute2,
         ca-certificates,
# unattended-upgrades: automatic security updates (Debian's default answer
# turns them on).
         unattended-upgrades,
         ${misc:Depends}
# Recommends: removable tools. The image installs them (config/hooks/normal/
# 0050-recommends); users can uninstall any of them without apt also
# removing this package.
Recommends: wpasupplicant,
            intel-microcode,
            amd64-microcode,
            bash-completion,
            iputils-ping,
            curl,
            man-db,
            manpages,
            less,
            nano,
            file,
            pciutils,
            usbutils,
# fsck.fat for the EFI system partition of installed UEFI systems.
            dosfstools,
            xz-utils,
            zstd
Description: Zyphor OS base system (metapackage)
 The parts every Zyphor OS edition has, including the console-only one:
 kernel, systemd, NetworkManager, sudo, locales and keyboard setup, and
 automatic security updates, plus common command-line tools.
